 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Training Collapse:** Direct image-space supervision can collapse to degenerate solutions where the Stage-1 feature is dominated by a single principal component (explaining >98% variance) [S1, unofficial]. POD prevents this by providing a better-conditioned target [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Non-Unique Inverse Mapping:** The mapping from residual images to Gaussian parameters is non-unique. This ambiguity is amplified across stages through error accumulation [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Negative Residuals:** The residual image $E_{i-1}$ may contain negative values, so the rendering loss must be evaluated on the accumulated rendering against the ground truth, not directly on the residual [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Training Collapse:** Direct image-space supervision is under-constrained and can collapse to degenerate solutions (e.g., Stage-1 feature dominated by a single principal component explaining 98.35% of variance) [S1, unofficial]. POD prevents this by providing a better-conditioned regression target [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Gradient Scale:** The Gaussian-space distillation loss must be scaled (e.g., multiplied by 100) to match the gradient scale of Gaussian parameter regression [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Residual Values:** The residual image $E_{i-1}$ may contain negative values, so SSIM must be evaluated on the accumulated rendering against the ground truth, not the residual itself [S1, unofficial].
 
